  "notes": "USD per 1M tokens from Anthropic Pricing docs. cache_write_per_m = 5-minute cache write (1.25× base input). 1h cache write is 2× (not stored as separate field). cache_read = 0.1× base. Sonnet 5 intro through 2026-08-31 as claude-sonnet-5-intro. Fast mode Opus 4.8 and Opus 5 are a mode not a separate model id ($10/$50, ~2× price/~2.5× speed) — see claims in capabilities. model.claude-sonnet-5-intro.valid_until=2026-08-31 (machine field). Opus 5 pricing matches Opus 4.8 ($5/$25); 1M ctx, 128k max output (300k via batch beta). 2026-09-05 refresh: claude-sonnet-5 CHANGED 3/0.3/3.75/15 -> 2/0.2/2.5/10. Vendor note verbatim: \"The $2/$10 per million input/output token pricing for Claude Sonnet 5, announced at launch as introductory pricing through August 31, 2026, is now the standard price. The previously scheduled increase to $3/$15 per million input/output tokens on September 1, 2026 will not occur.\" The claude-sonnet-5-intro promo row is therefore DELETED rather than expired — it did not lapse, it became the standard rate, so retaining it as historical would misrepresent what happened. NEW: claude-fable-5-1 and claude-mythos-5-1 (10/50) whose cache reads are 0.025x base ($0.25), not the usual 0.1x. Re-verified UNCHANGED: opus-5, opus-4-8/4-7/4-6, fable-5, mythos-5, sonnet-4-6/4-5, haiku-4-5.",
